Supplement, 21 August 1913; pg. 348. "Mr. Brown played this game very well up
to a point, and then missed his way. Still, as he is quite blind, the
surprising is he did so well. He plays with a special board and set of men,
held on his knees, and has the ordinary pieces moved for him. The winner, Mr.
Whittard, is somewhere near 90 years of age, making it difficult to decide
which player was handicapped most." (TLS)} 0-1

